
-------------------------------------------------
1. Title
-------------------------------------------------

Week 3 Documentation
Student Average Calculator

-------------------------------------------------


-------------------------------------------------
2. Identify the Components
-------------------------------------------------

2.1 Inputs
1. Quiz 1 mark
2. Quiz 2 mark
3. Quiz 3 mark
4. User choice (Y/N)

-------------------------------------------------

2.2 Process
1. Receive quiz marks from the user.
2. Calculate the average mark.
3. Check if the average is greater than or equal to 50.
4. Display PASS if average is 50 or above.
5. Display FAIL if average is below 50.
6. Ask the user whether to continue.

-------------------------------------------------

3.3 Outputs
1. Average mark
2. PASS message
3. FAIL message
4. Program Ended message

-------------------------------------------------


-------------------------------------------------
3. Design the Algorithm
-------------------------------------------------

3.1 Pseudocode

START

Set choice = "Y"

WHILE choice == "Y"

    Input quiz1
    Input quiz2
    Input quiz3

    average = (quiz1 + quiz2 + quiz3) / 3

    Display average

    IF average >= 50 THEN
        Display "PASS"
    ELSE
        Display "FAIL"
    ENDIF

    Input choice

END WHILE

Display "Program Ended"

STOP

-------------------------------------------------


-------------------------------------------------
4. Algorithm Structure
-------------------------------------------------

4.1 Identify the Algorithm Structure
4.2 Sequence

Input quiz1
Input quiz2
Input quiz3

average = (quiz1 + quiz2 + quiz3) / 3

-------------------------------------------------

4.3 Explanation
The statements are executed one after 
another in order.

-------------------------------------------------


-------------------------------------------------
5. Selection
-------------------------------------------------

5.1 Selection

IF average >= 50
    Display "PASS"
ELSE
    Display "FAIL"
ENDIF

-------------------------------------------------

5.2 Explanation
The program chooses between two different actions 
based on the average mark.

-------------------------------------------------


-------------------------------------------------
6. Iteration
-------------------------------------------------

6.1 Iteration

WHILE choice == "Y"

    Repeat the process

END WHILE

-------------------------------------------------

6.2 Explanation
The loop repeats the program until the user enters N.

-------------------------------------------------


-------------------------------------------------
7. Conclusion
-------------------------------------------------

This program demonstrates the three basic control structures:

1. Sequence – entering marks and calculating average.
2. Selection – determining PASS or FAIL.
3. Iteration – repeating the program using a while loop.

The program calculates the student's average mark 
and displays the result accordingly.

-------------------------------------------------
